A||||7||camaro2fiero||The ole Iron Duke, Made my day||||6||
Z||000000||camaro2fiero||05-11-2001||11:14 PM||||I bought my 1984 2m4 about 1 month ago now.She is in excellent condition with 33500 miles. The other day I was coming home from the doctors,At a stop light i was waiting and beside me pulled up a 95+ Firebird.This car obviously had some modifications,I could tell this by the louder than normal idle, and aftermarket wing.The light turned green and I drove off as usual not gunning it but a modest take off from the light.I was ahead of the Firebird ,who must have thought I was trying to race.Next thing you know ,I hear the Firebird kick into passing gear and went roaring by me.I smiled thinking this guy thinks I am trying to race.Well we came to the next light and when it turned green I took off faster than the previous light .I had him beat until about 50 mph.He then blew by me .I was so proud of this little 4cyl making that Firebird have to catch me,even though I dont push her near 4500 let alone 5000.It was the highlight of the day.Anyways I thought I would share that with you all.Take Care fellow Fiero lovers||||reg||6
Z||000001||KRMFiero||05-11-2001||11:28 PM||||People may make fun of the duke but it really is a fun/quick engine, i like them||||reg||1
